From aeacf4ef49194948b50b8e1490d7af163eadaefa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yuanyuan Chen <cyyever@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 08:45:14 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] kosmickrisp: do not apply primitive restart to non-indexed
 draws

Primitive restart is scoped to indexed draws -- Vulkan 1.4, "Primitive
Restart": "This enable only applies to indexed draws".  kk_unroll_geometry
passes the restart index through whenever primitiveRestartEnable is set,
without checking that the draw is indexed.

For a non-indexed draw that is not a harmless no-op.  The unroll kernel
reads its input through poly_load_index(), which returns the vertex ID
itself when there is no index buffer (in_index_size_B == 0), and
poly_unroll_geometry() compares exactly that value against the restart
index.  The runtime's ia.primitive_restart_index stays 0 until an index
buffer is first bound (it is derived from the index type by
vk_cmd_set_index_buffer_type), so on such a draw vertex 0 reads as a
restart marker.  A 4-vertex triangle fan then emits one triangle instead
of two: the scan restarts at vertex 0, drops the hub, and decomposes only
vertices 1..3.  A fullscreen quad loses half of itself along its diagonal.

Triangle fans are the topology that reaches this, because they unroll
unconditionally (Metal has no fan primitive) and so never pass through
requires_unroll_restart(), which does scope restart to indexed draws.
Observed with DXVK, which enables primitiveRestartEnable for every
strip/fan topology, on Super Street Fighter IV's 2D screens.

Unroll non-indexed draws as if restart were disabled, matching
requires_unroll_restart().
---
 src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_cmd_draw.c | 18 ++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_cmd_draw.c b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_cmd_draw.c
index 2659321c..6d323b84 100644
--- a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_cmd_draw.c
+++ b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_cmd_draw.c
@@ -1482,8 +1482,22 @@ kk_unroll_geometry(struct kk_cmd_buffer *cmd, struct kk_draw_command *data)
       .in_draw = data->indirect_command.addr,
       .out_draw = out_draws.gpu,
       .in_draw_stride_el = data->indirect_command.stride / sizeof(uint32_t),
-      /* Handle primitive restart disable by forcing index to UINT32_MAX */
-      .restart_index = !data->restart ? UINT32_MAX : data->restart_index,
+      /* Handle primitive restart disable by forcing index to UINT32_MAX.
+       *
+       * Primitive restart applies to indexed draws only ("This enable only
+       * applies to indexed draws"), so a non-indexed draw must be unrolled as
+       * if restart were disabled however the flag is set. It cannot merely be
+       * ignored downstream: with no index buffer the unroll kernel's
+       * poly_load_index() returns the vertex ID itself, so a restart index of
+       * 0 -- what the runtime reports until an index buffer is first bound --
+       * makes vertex 0 restart the primitive. A 4-vertex triangle fan then
+       * emits one triangle instead of two, cutting a fullscreen quad in half
+       * along its diagonal. requires_unroll_restart() already scopes restart
+       * to indexed draws; fans reach here without passing through it, since
+       * they unroll unconditionally (Metal has no fan primitive).
+       */
+      .restart_index =
+         (!data->restart || !data->indexed) ? UINT32_MAX : data->restart_index,
       .index_buffer_size_el =
          data->indexed ? data->index_buffer.range / data->index_buffer_el_size_B
                        : 0u,
-- 
2.55.0

